# Vestie — architecture & patterns

> **Before every task:** read with `agent_workflow.mdc` and `pre_commit.mdc`.  
> **Reference implementation:** `lib/user/features/borrow/` (Week 8) + `lib/user/features/contribute/`.

Principal goal: **scalable, testable, team-ready** — widgets stay thin; business logic and I/O stay in domain/data.

---

## 1. Layer boundaries (strict)

```text
presentation/   → Cubit/Bloc, screens, widgets, UI mappers, route navigation helpers
domain/         → entities, repository interfaces, use cases (no Flutter, no Dio)
data/           → models, mappers, repository impl, remote/local data sources
```

| Layer | May import | Must NOT |
|-------|------------|----------|
| **presentation** | domain entities, use cases (via Cubit ctor/DI), `core/` UI utils | `Dio`, `DioClient`, raw JSON `Map`, `ApiConstants` in widgets |
| **domain** | `core/error`, `dartz` | Flutter, Dio, data models |
| **data** | domain, `ApiConstants`, `DioClient` | `BuildContext`, widgets |

**Shared cross-feature entities** (e.g. `BorrowRequestEntity` in `lib/features/project_detail/domain/entities/`) are allowed when multiple features render the same API shape.

---

## 2. Standard data flow (required for API features)

```text
Screen → Cubit/Bloc → UseCase → Repository → RemoteDataSource → DioClient
                ↑                      ↓
           emit state            Model.fromJson → Entity
```

1. **RemoteDataSource** — HTTP only; throws `ServerException` / `UnauthorizedException`.
2. **Repository impl** — catches exceptions → `Either<Failure, T>`; maps models → entities.
3. **Use case** — one public action per class; thin wrapper over repository.
4. **Cubit/Bloc** — calls use cases; maps failures via `FailureMapper`; holds loading/error UI state.
5. **Screen** — `BlocBuilder` / `BlocConsumer`; no business rules.

**Register** new use cases in `lib/core/di/inject_*.dart` + `service_locator.dart`.  
**Route-scoped Cubits** — create in `project_routes.dart` (or feature route group), not global singletons for form wizards.

---

## 3. No magic strings (product + wire)

Centralize literals — **never** scatter user-facing or API contract strings in widgets.

| Kind | Where |
|------|--------|
| User-visible copy | `AppStrings` |
| REST paths | `ApiConstants` |
| Routes | `AppRoutes` |
| Assets | `AppAssets` |
| API query/body keys | model `toJson` / `fromJson` in **data** layer |
| API enum values (`Pending`, `Agree`, `Approve`) | parse in **models**; expose typed fields/getters on **entities** — widgets compare `entity.isPending`, not `status == 'Pending'` |
| Deep links / redirect paths | `ApiConstants` or `core/constants/` |
| Validation messages | `AppStrings` or validator return values — not inline in `Text` |

**Bad:** `context.push('/project/borrow')`, `'Failed to load borrow'`, `if (status == 'Disbursed')` in a widget.  
**Good:** `AppRoutes.borrowFlow`, `FailureMapper.userMessage(failure)`, `summary.isRepayable` on entity.

When adding a new API field or status, extend the **model + entity** in the same change — do not leak raw JSON keys into presentation.

---

## 4. No magic numbers (layout + domain)

| Kind | Where |
|------|--------|
| Spacing, gutters, icon sizes (UI) | `AppDimens` if shared; else **`flutter_screenutil`** (`.w`, `.h`, `.r`, `.sp`) — base **390×844** |
| Border radius (repeated) | `AppRadius` or `.r` |
| Colors | `AppColors` — add a named token if Figma introduces a new color |
| Business limits (borrow cap, poll interval) | domain entity, API response, or named `static const` in **one** feature constants file — not inline in Cubit logic |
| Timeouts / retries | `core/network/` or feature data source — named constants |

**Bad:** `padding: EdgeInsets.all(17)`, `fontSize: 15`, `Color(0xFF1A1A1A)`, `await Future.delayed(Duration(milliseconds: 400))` for fake API.  
**Good:** `EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16.w)`, `fontSize: 16.sp`, `AppColors.grey1100`, real use case call.

Literal `0` / `1` for list indices or `flex: 1` are fine. Prefer named getters for non-obvious numeric domain rules (e.g. `args.borrowLimit`).

