## 6. UI patterns

- Wrappers: `AppText`, `AppButton`, `AppTextField`, `AppToast` — not raw Material + `ScaffoldMessenger`.
- **Validation** in `ValidationUtils` or Cubit — not in widget `onChanged`.
- **Leader vs member UI** — `lib/leader/features/` vs `lib/user/features/`; shared shells in `lib/features/`.

### Post-auth flow screen shell (gradient + scroll + pinned CTA)

Use this layout for **form / action flows** under `PostAuthGradientBackground` (Edit Profile, My Borrow, repay confirm, etc.). **Do not** apply to **`AppSuccessScreen`** — success screens use their own full-screen pattern with **no** post-gradient header.

**Reference:** `lib/features/profile/presentation/pages/edit_profile_screen.dart`

```text
Scaffold(backgroundColor: transparent, resizeToAvoidBottomInset: false)
  PostAuthGradientBackground
    Column
      PostAuthFlowSubHeader  (or ProfileSubHeader — same widget)
      Expanded
        SingleChildScrollView / ListView
          padding: AppDimens.postAuthFlowScrollPadding   // 20.w L/R, 16.h bottom
          child: content only — no extra outer padding in body widgets
      FlowScreenFooter (when screen has a primary CTA)
        AppButton — pinned, never inside scroll
```

| Piece | Rule |
|-------|------|
| Header | `PostAuthFlowSubHeader` — default `PostAuthHeader` padding; back `AppColors.textPrimary` |
| Scroll body | `AppDimens.postAuthFlowScrollPadding` on the **screen** scroll view |
| List-only (no footer button) | `FlowScreenFooterInsets.listPadding(context)` — same `20.w` horizontal |
| Footer CTA | **`FlowScreenFooter`** + `AppButton` — uses `FlowScreenFooterInsets` (`20.w` horizontal, `max(24.h, systemBottom + 8.h)`). **Never** `SafeArea(top: false)` + fixed `16.h`/`20.h` bottom padding |
| Keyboard forms | **Pinned footer:** `resizeToAvoidBottomInset: false` + scroll `AppDimens.postAuthFlowScrollPaddingWithKeyboard(context)` (Edit Profile, create project, voting window, announcements). **Amount entry:** keep `resizeToAvoidBottomInset: true` + `FlowScreenFooter` (borrow/contribute/deposit amount) — do not change keyboard behavior when syncing visuals |
| Body widgets | Column/content only — **no** duplicate `SingleChildScrollView` or screen-level padding inside `widgets/` |

**Anti-pattern:** pinned CTA inside `SingleChildScrollView`, or `bottomNavigationBar` / `SafeArea` with ad-hoc `EdgeInsets.only(bottom: 14.h)` — causes buttons under the system nav bar on some devices.

**Performance:** reuse `FlowScreenFooter` / `FlowScreenFooterInsets` only — no per-screen `MediaQuery` math, no extra `LayoutBuilder` shells for footer spacing.

### Loading & screen freeze (production)

Every async user action that hits the API must show feedback and **block duplicate submits**. Pick **one** pattern per interaction — do not leave POST taps with only `enabled: false` and no visible loader.

| Situation | Widget | Cubit flag (example) | Reference |
|-----------|--------|----------------------|-----------|
| **Initial screen / list load** | Named shimmer from `app_shimmer_lists.dart` | `loading` | `MyBorrowRequestShimmer`, `PaymentCardListShimmer` |
| **Initial load failed** | `AppErrorView` + **Try Again** (`onRetry` → Cubit `load()`) — **not** empty state + toast | `loadFailed` getter on state | `my_borrow_request_screen`, `borrow_repay_payment_options_screen` |
| **Cross-route async** (e.g. repay auto-skip) | Keep footer `AppButton.isLoading` until navigation helper returns | `startingRepay` through full `startRepayFlow` | `my_borrow_request_screen` + `BorrowRepayNavigation` |
| **Pinned footer POST** (submit, confirm, cancel CTA on screen) | `AppButton(isLoading: true)` + `onPressed: null` while busy | `loading`, `submitting`, `cancelling` | `borrow_flow_screen`, `borrow_repay_confirm_screen` |
| **Dialog confirm POST** (approve, reject, cancel confirm) | `AppActionDialog.showAsync` — spinner on primary, secondary disabled, `PopScope` blocks back while loading | return `Future<bool>` from dialog `onPrimary` | `borrow_request_decision_dialogs`, `cancel_borrow_request_dialog` |
| **Row / card tap POST** (vote, payment-method preview) | `AppLoadingOverlay` on the screen body **or** inline loader on the control (`AppVoteButtons.isLoading`) | `selecting`, `isVoting` | `borrow_repay_payment_options_screen`, `borrow_request_card` |
| **Background refresh** (keep content visible) | `AppLoadingOverlay` on existing body | `silentRefreshing` | `notifications_screen` |

**Rules:**

1. Cubit owns the busy flag — emit `true` before the use case, `false` on success/failure; guard re-entry (`if (state.submitting) return`).
2. **`AppButton.isLoading`** — only for the **single** pinned footer CTA; keeps label area as spinner; button stays visually active (see `AppButton` implementation).
3. **`AppLoadingOverlay`** — `AbsorbPointer` + centred loader; use when there is no single footer button to own the loader (payment row tap, silent refresh). On **post-gradient** screens: `scrimColor: AppColors.postAuthLoadingOverlayScrim` (transparent — no dim box) and wrap the full `Column` (header + `Expanded` body) so the overlay does not split header vs list. On opaque list surfaces (e.g. notifications silent refresh), default dark `modalBarrier` scrim is fine.
4. **`AppActionDialog.showAsync`** — for any dialog whose primary action calls an API; return `true`/`false` only after POST **and** any required project-detail reload (see §5 post-action sync); show success dialog **after** `showAsync` returns `true` — never show success before those complete.
5. **Do not** use bare `CircularProgressIndicator` for full-screen first load — use a named shimmer. Small inline spinners inside `AppButton`, `_DialogButton`, or `AppVoteButtons` are fine.
6. **Do not** use `setState` for submit loading — Cubit/Bloc only.
7. **POST submit failure on confirm step** — show inline error + retry hint on the screen; **`AppToast.showError`** only for earlier steps. **Back** clears idempotency key when user edits amount/terms.
8. **Toast vs full error** — use `listenWhen` to skip toast when `loadFailed` is true (full-screen `AppErrorView` already shown). Background list reload failures stay silent (keep stale data).
9. **Transient feedback** — **`AppToast.showError` / `showSuccess` / `showInfo`** only. **Do not** use `AppSnackBar` or `ScaffoldMessenger.showSnackBar` in new code.
10. **Confirm CTA gating** — pinned **Confirm / Submit** stays **`onPressed: null`** until required checkboxes (terms / non-refundable) **and** payment source are valid (wallet covers total **or** card selected; deposit: card required). Show inline validation under **`AppPaymentMethodPill`** (`hasError` + message) — do not rely on enabled button + toast for missing switch/card.

### Error handling (every API feature)

```text
RemoteDataSource throws → Repository → Either<Failure, T> → UseCase → Cubit
                                                              ↓
                                    FailureMapper.userMessage(failure) on state
                                                              ↓
              loadFailed? → AppErrorView + retry    else action error? → AppToast.showError
```

| Failure type | UI |
|--------------|-----|
| Initial `GET` / screen load | `AppErrorView` + Try Again — **no toast** |
| Row tap / submit / cancel / vote / decide | `AppToast.showError` (or inline on confirm step) |
| Validation before API (confirm tap) | `AppToast.showError` with `AppStrings` message |
| Forbidden / navigation guard | `AppToast.showError` with `AppStrings.errorForbidden` |
| Success after POST | Success dialog / `AppSuccessScreen` — optional `AppToast.showSuccess` when no dedicated success UI |

**Cubit rules:** emit `loading`/`submitting`/… before await; map all failures with **`FailureMapper.userMessage`**; expose `loadFailed` when the screen has no partial data to show.

### Idempotency keys (money POST)

| Flow | When to create key | Reuse on retry | Clear when |
|------|-------------------|----------------|------------|
| Borrow create | Entering confirm step (`toConfirm` success) | Same key on Submit retries until success | `backToAmount` |
| Borrow repay | `BorrowRepayConfirmCubit` construction | Same key on Confirm retries until success | New Cubit per confirm route |
| Contribute / deposit / withdraw | Per existing feature patterns | Header or body per API contract | — |

Send borrow create via `Idempotency-Key` header; repay via body `idempotencyKey` (Week 8 API). Generate with `newIdempotencyKey('borrow'|'repay')` — **never** regenerate on retry within the same confirm session.

Prefer **Cubit** for use-case calls from UI. `ServiceLocator.instance` directly inside widgets is legacy — match nearby code when editing, but new flows should inject use cases through Cubit constructors.

